{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1354260-the-dracon-s-hunt-of-the-carpathian-tzimisce","id":1354260,"title":"The dracon's hunt of the carpathian Tzimisce","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-10T16:18:55-08:00","id":1354260,"title":"The dracon's hunt of the carpathian Tzimisce","content":"So after the disastrous embrace of Gesu. The Dracon went batshit crazy. I was wondering if there is more information out there about the dracon's hunt of the carpathian Tzimisce? (other then what is written in the wiki).<br /> <br /> How badly were the carphatian Tzimisce hurt by his actions? How many elders were destroyed? What were the exact details of Gesu's embrace? How did his final battle with Triglav occur? Why didn't Yorak interfer when his clanmates were being butchered? Any theories would also be good to hear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T16:23:45-08:00","id":1354262,"title":"","content":"The Dracon killed Triglav the Three Header (another childe of the Eldest) in his rampage, triggering a blood feud between both lineages. Let's also have in mind that when this happened, it was also around the same time that Samiel destroyed the Eldest for the first time (that we know of) and then he was reborn in the Dracon's womb. This led him to take care of his sire back to his haven in Cyprus. Most of this is between Clanbook Tzimisce revised (destruction of Samiel), Dark Ages Europe/Road of Heaven (date in which the youngest childe of Samiel was embraced) and Dark Ages novel Tzimisce (the clan blood feud)<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T10:46:52-08:00","id":1354611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1354260-the-dracon-s-hunt-of-the-carpathian-tzimisce?p=1354262#post1354262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dracon killed Triglav the Three Header (another childe of the Eldest) in his rampage, triggering a blood feud between both lineages. Let's also have in mind that when this happened, it was also around the same time that Samiel destroyed the Eldest for the first time (that we know of) and then he was reborn in the Dracon's womb. This led him to take care of his sire back to his haven in Cyprus. Most of this is between Clanbook Tzimisce revised (destruction of Samiel), Dark Ages Europe/Road of Heaven (date in which the youngest childe of Samiel was embraced) and Dark Ages novel Tzimisce (the clan blood feud)<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's keep in mind that Samiel and the Tzimisce Antediluvian killing each other and the latter reforming in the body of the Dracon is not a fact but rather a story told my a 20th century Tzimisce in character. She relates a theory some Tzimisce hold as a fact but that's so only if you choose for it to be in your chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T11:06:19-08:00","id":1354619,"title":"","content":"In Dark Ages: Novel Tzimisce it's said that Velya the Viviseccionist is the only survivor of the purge of the Triglav's offspring. But Shaagra of Prague is another childe of Triglav. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2250-magus","name":"Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T13:37:11-08:00","id":1354656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1354260-the-dracon-s-hunt-of-the-carpathian-tzimisce?p=1354619#post1354619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Dark Ages: Novel Tzimisce it's said that Velya the Viviseccionist is the only survivor of the purge of the Triglav's offspring. But Shaagra of Prague is another childe of Triglav.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Interesting, so the dracon pretty much wiped out Triglav's entire line. I did not know that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T13:44:12-08:00","id":1354661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1354260-the-dracon-s-hunt-of-the-carpathian-tzimisce?p=1354611#post1354611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's keep in mind that Samiel and the Tzimisce Antediluvian killing each other and the latter reforming in the body of the Dracon is not a fact but rather a story told my a 20th century Tzimisce in character. She relates a theory some Tzimisce hold as a fact but that's so only if you choose for it to be in your chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It always seemed a bit strange that Samiel took out an Antediluvian in single combat. And not just any Antediluvian, probably the most powerful of them all. It would make sense if it is just a story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T15:02:03-08:00","id":1354675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1354260-the-dracon-s-hunt-of-the-carpathian-tzimisce?p=1354619#post1354619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Dark Ages: Novel Tzimisce it's said that Velya the Viviseccionist is the only survivor of the purge of the Triglav's offspring. But Shaagra of Prague is another childe of Triglav.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It is believed that Shaagra herself never knew her sire Triglav, and that might be why she was left apart of the blood feud.<br /> <br /> Kosczecsyku is a childe of Triglav according to the lineage of Osobei Vasilevitch, something whoever wrote V20 Rites of the Blood forgot about and wrote him under Yorak's lineage.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T16:05:55-08:00","id":1354691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1354260-the-dracon-s-hunt-of-the-carpathian-tzimisce?p=1354661#post1354661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It always seemed a bit strange that Samiel took out an Antediluvian in single combat. And not just any Antediluvian, probably the most powerful of them all. It would make sense if it is just a story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. I truly think the Eldest has a thing for getting &quot;killed&quot;. Like, it's their kink. Sure, it never truly dies, but it gets off on letting others think it dies, just to come back later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T04:26:01-08:00","id":1354748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kosczecsyku is a childe of Triglav according to the lineage of Osobei Vasilevitch, something whoever wrote V20 Rites of the Blood forgot about and wrote him under Yorak's lineage.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. I remenber that in &quot;The Bitter Crusade&quot; there's a chapter with some Tzimisce, and it's mentioned the war between the Children of the Dracon and the rest of the clan.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2250-magus","name":"Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T01:13:17-08:00","id":1355794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1354260-the-dracon-s-hunt-of-the-carpathian-tzimisce?p=1354661#post1354661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It always seemed a bit strange that Samiel took out an Antediluvian in single combat. And not just any Antediluvian, probably the most powerful of them all. It would make sense if it is just a story.</div> </div> </div> </div>He didn't. As mighty as he was, Samiel killed the then vessel of The Eldest. But, as the first Tzimisce childer knew, they were just vessels for The Eldest's ressurection , if required. Nothing more. If a single drop of The Eldest's blood exists, he lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25666,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","user":"Illuminostro","date":". 12-19-2019, 04:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T10:09:19-08:00","id":1355881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1354260-the-dracon-s-hunt-of-the-carpathian-tzimisce?p=1355794#post1355794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He didn't. As mighty as he was, Samiel killed the then vessel of The Eldest. But, as the first Tzimisce childer knew, they were just vessels for The Eldest's ressurection , if required. Nothing more. If a single drop of The Eldest's blood exists, he lives.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Antedilluvian managed to ressurect himself because of his unique ability to reform himself within the body of any of his childer. But Samiel bested him in single combat (or it was a draw). The Tzimisce Antedilluvian with all his power couldn't prevent the destruction of his vessel at the time. It took him decades (if not more) to come back from that. That just shows that the eldest of the Methuselahs aren't that much weaker then the Antedilluvians. Or maybe Samiel was just that powerful. Also it's worth remembering that if it was any other Antediluvian they would have, most likely, met final death in that encounter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24527,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","user":"blackshade","date":". 12-19-2019, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T11:34:38-08:00","id":1355902,"title":"","content":"I haven't read clan novels or much of the Dark Ages line to confirm, but I had the impression that Samiel was presented as a &quot;holy warrior&quot; type figure, implying that True Faith may have played an important role in that battle. That could make up for a lot of power differential, particularly against an opponent as inhuman and evil as the Eldest Fiend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T14:04:30-08:00","id":1355939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1354260-the-dracon-s-hunt-of-the-carpathian-tzimisce?p=1355902#post1355902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't read clan novels or much of the Dark Ages line to confirm, but I had the impression that Samiel was presented as a &quot;holy warrior&quot; type figure, implying that True Faith may have played an important role in that battle. That could make up for a lot of power differential, particularly against an opponent as inhuman and evil as the Eldest Fiend.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the Dark Ages Novel: Tzimisce the Dracon remembers his sire. He says that the Antediluvian was more human before his &quot;destruction&quot; and the resurrection &quot;failed&quot; in some way because the Antediluvian became in a different, inhuman creature. It's an interesting premise because it would indicate that Tzimisce was not always a monster.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2250-magus","name":"Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-11T19:19:00-08:00","id":1360423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1354260-the-dracon-s-hunt-of-the-carpathian-tzimisce?p=1355881#post1355881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The Antedilluvian managed to ressurect himself because of his unique ability to reform himself within the body of any of his childer. But Samiel bested him in single combat (or it was a draw). The Tzimisce Antedilluvian with all his power couldn't prevent the destruction of his vessel at the time. It took him decades (if not more) to come back from that. That just shows that the eldest of the Methuselahs aren't that much weaker then the Antedilluvians. Or maybe Samiel was just that powerful. Also it's worth remembering that if it was any other Antediluvian they would have, most likely, met final death in that encounter.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I stated &quot;He didn't,&quot; I meant that Samiel didn't kill Tzimisce. Not really. He just killed that physical form. As long as any thing has Tzimisce's blood in them, it can reform itself.<br /> <br /> So, we are in agreement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T04:31:57-08:00","id":1360493,"title":"","content":"I wonder how canon the Vukodlak is given that Shagara is the &quot;canonical&quot; holder of his territory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-13T11:56:12-08:00","id":1360724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1354260-the-dracon-s-hunt-of-the-carpathian-tzimisce?p=1360493#post1360493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder how canon the Vukodlak is given that Shagara is the &quot;canonical&quot; holder of his territory.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Who is he/she/it?<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-13T12:25:25-08:00","id":1360732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1354260-the-dracon-s-hunt-of-the-carpathian-tzimisce?p=1360724#post1360724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Who is he/she/it?<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampire: The Masquerade: Redemption's villain. A millennia old Tzimisce of the 5th Generation who had a massive cult to it. All vampires in Prague worshiped it and it lived in Shagara's castle, replacing her.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Vukodlak\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Vukodlak</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-31T12:36:47-07:00","id":1552780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1354260-the-dracon-s-hunt-of-the-carpathian-tzimisce?p=1355939#post1355939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the Dark Ages Novel: Tzimisce the Dracon remembers his sire.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I took the idea this change as being the 'fact' that the Eldest, born to the Dracon, grew in Yorak's Cathedral of Flesh, and that gestation left the Eldest twisted. However...<br /> <br /> As stated, the whole story of the Dracon birthing the Eldest is just that, a story. By the same token, <b>Vampire: The Masquerade</b> has ever shown the folly of seeing memory as history. The entirety of the <i>Book of Nod</i> is a testament (no pun intended) to that, in fact. The notion that the Dracon annihilated Triglav's line falls well into this dubious valley of 'truth.' All of which means that if any truth can be a lie, every lie may be true. Thus making any neonate's search for meaning in this un-dead existence difficult, to say the least. <br /> <br /> Postscriptum: I love these kinds of discussions!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-01T08:53:02-07:00","id":1552805,"title":"","content":"I was under the impression that Vukodlak -was- Shaagra and it was just a psuedonym or title, seeing as a Vukodlak is a type of Slavic werewolf. It was less that it was Vukodlak, but THE Vukodlak. There is also that fact that we meet Libussa, who is Shaagra's child and ghoul in the books and serves the same function. <br /> <br /> They're both the same age and generation, and seeing as Vukodlak was creating its own Cathedral of Flesh near the end of the game, brings together the connection of being Yorak's protege that Shaagra was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-03T21:44:44-07:00","id":1552864,"title":"","content":"In regards to Gesu embrace. The Dracon was visited by a group of Tzismce and including one who seemed to be a envoy of the eldest who warned him that embracing Gesu would be a mistake.<br /> <br /> The Dracon ignored them and viewed them as superstitious fools, but when he embraced his childe, Gesu immediately went into a toporid state and stayed that way for some time.<br /> <br /> Dracon thought that his clan mates put a curse on the embrace and went on the warpath. Afterwards when he came back Gesu awoke from his topor and embraced his brother Symeon who was promised to the Ventrue Antonius and began the end of the Trinity's dream.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 08-04-2025, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-20T16:40:39-07:00","id":1553307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1354260-the-dracon-s-hunt-of-the-carpathian-tzimisce?p=1355881#post1355881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The Antedilluvian managed to ressurect himself because of his unique ability to reform himself within the body of any of his childer. But Samiel bested him in single combat (or it was a draw). The Tzimisce Antedilluvian with all his power couldn't prevent the destruction of his vessel at the time. It took him decades (if not more) to come back from that. That just shows that the eldest of the Methuselahs aren't that much weaker then the Antedilluvians. Or maybe Samiel was just that powerful. Also it's worth remembering that if it was any other Antediluvian they would have, most likely, met final death in that encounter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Eldest did come back long enough to beat the crap out of Lugoj and take his place for a time too, no? So not exactly that long depending on how one counts timescales.<br /> <br /> But yeah, i agree that sometimes a fight between an antediluvian and a methuselah does not have to be a curbstomp by for the former, specially depending on what each one favors, style of play/combat, etc. Sometimes the younger kindred is the paper to your rock, or rock to your scissors, so to speak.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1354260-the-dracon-s-hunt-of-the-carpathian-tzimisce?p=1552805#post1552805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was under the impression that Vukodlak -was- Shaagra and it was just a psuedonym or title, seeing as a Vukodlak is a type of Slavic werewolf. It was less that it was Vukodlak, but THE Vukodlak. There is also that fact that we meet Libussa, who is Shaagra's child and ghoul in the books and serves the same function.<br /> <br /> They're both the same age and generation, and seeing as Vukodlak was creating its own Cathedral of Flesh near the end of the game, brings together the connection of being Yorak's protege that Shaagra was.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vukodlak definitely fits in a setting space that is very much occupied by Shaagra in DA canon and can definitely see an argument for playing it as a persona of hers, gender-flipped or not.<br /> <br /> In my own games i made him into a 6th gen childe of Shaagra acting as her steward/representative of sorts, while in fact advancing a bunch of bizarre personal agendas (that i did some expansion and rework upon) utterly unrelated to her actual desires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-20-2025, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}